    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1039">

                <pb facs="0779" n="663" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg663"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 125.8273/41.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 11, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Joseph A. Marchani, clerk in American Consulate, Saltillo, arrived here this
                    morning. Reports all Americans reported arrested now released with exception
                    Vice Consul Silliman. Marchani left Saltillo May 8; states was taken from jail
                    to Consulate under heavy guard and compelled under threat of death open safe and
                    deliver all records including Red Code and three hundred pesos and jewelry left
                    at Consulate for safe keeping. Believes copies of Red Code being made for
                    distribution among federal officers. Consulate now held by guard of hundred
                    federals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
